{
  "video": {
    "id": "2TL8rY9Rc_A",
    "title": "Lac operon | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2TL8rY9Rc_A",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 324,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 92,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 7.07,
      "end": 7.71,
      "duration": 0.64,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Hi."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 7.71,
      "end": 9.9,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "In this clip we're going to demonstrate the gene"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 9.9,
      "end": 12.46,
      "duration": 2.56,
      "text": "regulation of the E. coli lac operon."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 12.46,
      "end": 15.26,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "As you remember from the lecture clips, the lac operon"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 15.26,
      "end": 18.12,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "is a collection of genes that produces the lactose"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 18.12,
      "end": 20.99,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "metabolism machinery when expressed."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 20.99,
      "end": 24.08,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "Now, when these are expressed, E. coli is able"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 24.08,
      "end": 25.66,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "to metabolize lactose."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 25.66,
      "end": 29.07,
      "duration": 3.41,
      "text": "However, it prefers to metabolize glucose, to use"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 29.07,
      "end": 30.51,
      "duration": 1.44,
      "text": "that as its sugar."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 30.51,
      "end": 34.71,
      "duration": 4.2,
      "text": "Thus, when there's glucose available to the cell, it's"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 34.71,
      "end": 39.48,
      "duration": 4.77,
      "text": "pointless for it to create this machinery, because it's"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 39.48,
      "end": 41.0,
      "duration": 1.52,
      "text": "not going to actually use it."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 41.0,
      "end": 43.78,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "It's going to metabolize the glucose instead."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 43.78,
      "end": 47.31,
      "duration": 3.53,
      "text": "But when we remove glucose and add lactose, the E. coli"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 47.31,
      "end": 50.89,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "absolutely needs to be able to metabolize this lactose,"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 50.89,
      "end": 53.08,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "otherwise it's not going to be able to grow with the"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 53.08,
      "end": 55.28,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "available energy source."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 55.28,
      "end": 59.37,
      "duration": 4.09,
      "text": "Thus, we have a couple of different situations."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 59.37,
      "end": 64.65,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "When we have glucose present but not lactose, we do not"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 64.65,
      "end": 68.95,
      "duration": 4.3,
      "text": "want to express the lac operon."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 68.95,
      "end": 73.69,
      "duration": 4.74,
      "text": "However, when we remove glucose and we add lactose, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 73.69,
      "end": 78.62,
      "duration": 4.93,
      "text": "do want to express the lac operon."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 78.62,
      "end": 83.25,
      "duration": 4.63,
      "text": "Now we've covered when the E. coli would like to express"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 83.25,
      "end": 84.3,
      "duration": 1.05,
      "text": "this operon."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 84.3,
      "end": 88.6,
      "duration": 4.3,
      "text": "However, how can it express this operon only when it wants"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 88.6,
      "end": 90.61,
      "duration": 2.01,
      "text": "to and not when it doesn't?"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 90.61,
      "end": 94.0,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "That's where the promoter comes into play."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 94.0,
      "end": 97.35,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "The promoter is where RNA polymerase binds."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 97.35,
      "end": 100.44,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "And RNA polymerase needs to bind to this promoter in order"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 100.44,
      "end": 104.85,
      "duration": 4.41,
      "text": "to transcribe and express these genes."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 104.85,
      "end": 108.55,
      "duration": 3.7,
      "text": "In this particular promoter, we have a site where a"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 108.55,
      "end": 112.48,
      "duration": 3.93,
      "text": "repressor can bind and a site where an activator can bind."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 112.48,
      "end": 118.81,
      "duration": 6.33,
      "text": "So I have a repressor and I have an activator."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 122.13,
      "end": 127.92,
      "duration": 5.79,
      "text": "So when the repressor is bound, polymerase cannot bind"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 127.92,
      "end": 129.65,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "to the promoter."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 129.65,
      "end": 133.24,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "Polymerase also needs the activator to be bound to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 133.24,
      "end": 135.64,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "promoter in order to bind."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 135.64,
      "end": 138.91,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "So how can the E. coli regulate when the repressor"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 138.91,
      "end": 141.71,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "and activator are bound to the promoter?"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 141.71,
      "end": 147.21,
      "duration": 5.5,
      "text": "Well, when we have lactose in the system, I have lactose"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 147.21,
      "end": 151.51,
      "duration": 4.3,
      "text": "right here, the repressor is able to bind lactose."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 151.51,
      "end": 153.83,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "The repressor only binds to the promoter"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 153.83,
      "end": 155.24,
      "duration": 1.41,
      "text": "when there is no lactose."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 155.24,
      "end": 160.13,
      "duration": 4.89,
      "text": "And when binding to lactose, the repressor comes undone"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 160.13,
      "end": 161.38,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "from the promoter."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 163.24,
      "end": 165.97,
      "duration": 2.73,
      "text": "How does the cell tell whether there's glucose"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 165.97,
      "end": 167.76,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "in the cell or not?"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 167.76,
      "end": 171.21,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "When glucose is low in the cell, the cell makes a"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 171.21,
      "end": 173.99,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "molecule called cyclic AMP, or CAMP."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 173.99,
      "end": 177.16,
      "duration": 3.17,
      "text": "I have a molecule of CAMP right here."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 177.16,
      "end": 180.21,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "And so CAMP is the cell's way of indicating that there is"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 180.21,
      "end": 182.7,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "low glucose in the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 182.7,
      "end": 185.64,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "The activator needs CAMP to bind to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 185.64,
      "end": 187.94,
      "duration": 2.3,
      "text": "activator binding site."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 187.94,
      "end": 191.73,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "When CAMP is removed, or glucose is added, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 191.73,
      "end": 196.44,
      "duration": 4.71,
      "text": "activator cannot bind to the promoter anymore."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 196.44,
      "end": 199.24,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "Ok, so let's give it a try."
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 199.24,
      "end": 204.01,
      "duration": 4.77,
      "text": "In this first situation we have glucose,"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 204.01,
      "end": 206.0,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "we don't have lactose."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 206.0,
      "end": 211.415,
      "duration": 5.415,
      "text": "So I have neither my lactose nor my CAMP in the system."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 216.44,
      "end": 218.39,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "Repressor, can you bind?"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 218.39,
      "end": 219.65,
      "duration": 1.26,
      "text": "The Repressor is bound."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 219.65,
      "end": 221.14,
      "duration": 1.49,
      "text": "Activator, can you bind?"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 221.14,
      "end": 223.5,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "No, the activator is not bound."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 223.5,
      "end": 228.18,
      "duration": 4.68,
      "text": "The repressor is bound, and so when RNA polymerase comes to"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 228.18,
      "end": 231.49,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "the promoter, RNA polymerase is not able to"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 231.49,
      "end": 233.93,
      "duration": 2.44,
      "text": "bind at this promoter."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 233.93,
      "end": 237.14,
      "duration": 3.21,
      "text": "And thus, it's not able to express these genes."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 239.8,
      "end": 244.85,
      "duration": 5.05,
      "text": "And so, as we can see here, there is no expression."
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 244.85,
      "end": 248.74,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "In this second situation, we have no glucose"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 248.74,
      "end": 251.77,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "and we do have lactose."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 251.77,
      "end": 257.18,
      "duration": 5.41,
      "text": "Since I'm removing glucose, I am adding back CAMP."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 257.18,
      "end": 258.95,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "Activator, can you bind?"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 258.95,
      "end": 260.73,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "Activator is now bound."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 260.73,
      "end": 264.145,
      "duration": 3.415,
      "text": "And I'm also adding lactose to the system."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 266.82,
      "end": 269.79,
      "duration": 2.97,
      "text": "Repressor can't bind anymore."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 269.79,
      "end": 271.82,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "So what do I have at my promoter now?"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 271.82,
      "end": 274.48,
      "duration": 2.66,
      "text": "RNA polymerase comes along and finds only an"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 274.48,
      "end": 276.15,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "activator at the promoter."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 276.15,
      "end": 280.08,
      "duration": 3.93,
      "text": "The polymerase can thus bind to the promoter and move"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 280.08,
      "end": 284.77,
      "duration": 4.69,
      "text": "downstream to transcribe and express the lactose metabolism"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 284.77,
      "end": 286.27,
      "duration": 1.5,
      "text": "machinery that we have here."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 293.11,
      "end": 299.4,
      "duration": 6.29,
      "text": "So we have now covered how the E. coli organism is able to"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 299.4,
      "end": 303.29,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "regulate the transcription of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 303.29,
      "end": 305.59,
      "duration": 2.3,
      "text": "lactose metabolism machinery."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 305.59,
      "end": 309.71,
      "duration": 4.12,
      "text": "This is only one example of many genes and many organisms"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 309.71,
      "end": 313.05,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "that are regulated by mechanisms such as this."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 313.05,
      "end": 316.32,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "Gene regulation is a very widespread mechanism, in order"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 316.32,
      "end": 318.95,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "to keep a cell from producing proteins that"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 318.95,
      "end": 320.82,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "are a waste to produce."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 320.82,
      "end": 322.07,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Thank you for watching."
    }
  ],
